WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.750
- Our first on today's
Twitter questionnaire

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.485
comes from David Covucci, I think?

00:00:06.485 --> 00:00:09.460
"Everyone is talking about
good quarantine habits,

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.668
tell me your worst.

00:00:10.668 --> 00:00:14.950
I for one have started chewing
nicotine gum for no reason,

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:18.048
other than it was on
sale at the pharmacy."

00:00:18.048 --> 00:00:18.881
What?

00:00:18.881 --> 00:00:19.757
(laughing)

00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:21.680
I want your life David,

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.405
'cause obviously not a lot is
going on, and I'm very busy.

00:00:25.405 --> 00:00:29.293
I don't, what's your worst
quarantine habit, Seth?

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.260
- I dunno, I think I'm
over-flossing, just to like,

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.783
break up the day.

00:00:34.783 --> 00:00:35.616
(laughing)

00:00:35.616 --> 00:00:36.449
- Oh my!

00:00:36.449 --> 00:00:37.282
You know what I'm doing?

00:00:37.282 --> 00:00:38.170
Q-tips.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.450
I already am a Q-tip queen,
I love cleaning my ears,

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.710
I can't stand, I can't stand like,

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.110
any kind of moisture in my ears.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.331
And I've been showering a lot,
'cause we live on a ranch.

00:00:46.331 --> 00:00:50.737
And I'm probably going
to ruin my ears, somehow.

00:00:50.737 --> 00:00:54.071
- Look, I love a good Q-tip
but I like to savor it.

00:00:54.071 --> 00:00:56.120
When I feel like over-using a Q-tip,

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.010
takes away the excitement.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.222
For me it's a treat.

00:00:59.222 --> 00:01:00.055
(laughing)

00:01:00.055 --> 00:01:00.888
It's like very...

00:01:00.888 --> 00:01:02.750
You know, if I accomplish something,

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:04.620
then I'm like, "You
grab yourself a Q-tip."

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.490
- Yeah.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.517
I love cleaning out my ears, okay.

00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:09.402
- Can I ask you a Q-tip question?

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.235
- Yes.

00:01:10.235 --> 00:01:13.550
- Do you one Q-tip that
you switch for each ear?

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.440
Or does each ear get one Q-tip?

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:16.680
- Here's the weird thing about me,

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.220
it's so interesting you asked.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.740
I do one Q-tip, and I do one side,

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.330
and then I do the other side deep-in.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:26.630
And then I take another
Q-tip and I do like, around,

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:27.518
you know, inside the ear.

00:01:27.518 --> 00:01:28.351
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:28.351 --> 00:01:29.626
- And then I do the same
thing with the other side.

00:01:29.626 --> 00:01:30.626
- Wow.

00:01:30.626 --> 00:01:32.071
- Yeah, it's a process.

00:01:32.071 --> 00:01:33.220
- Yeah.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.809
- I enjoy Q-tips, I call them,
"Ear-gasms", they're good.

00:01:35.809 --> 00:01:36.642
- There you go.

00:01:36.642 --> 00:01:37.653
- We may wanna not put that in the show.

00:01:37.653 --> 00:01:38.486
(laughing)

00:01:38.486 --> 00:01:40.173
or, I don't know, hell, put it in!

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.883
All right, the next one
is from @HelloCullen.

00:01:44.732 --> 00:01:47.840
"What if Seinfeld met the Sopranos?"

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.320
(laughing)

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.372
That is actually a great question!

00:01:51.372 --> 00:01:52.730
- Just like, what, what happened?

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:54.710
- [Kelly] Yeah, like, what,
so Seth, what do you think?

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:55.770
Turf war?

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:56.691
Like I'm just saying--

00:01:56.691 --> 00:01:57.524
- I dunno.

00:01:57.524 --> 00:01:59.450
I think like, Jerry would
be like, "what's the deal

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:01.059
with Pauly Walnuts?"

00:02:01.059 --> 00:02:02.663
(laughing)

00:02:02.663 --> 00:02:03.515
- Why?

00:02:03.515 --> 00:02:04.950
- "Why is the side of his hair white?"

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.722
- I think it would be more
interesting to see Kramer

00:02:06.722 --> 00:02:07.960
with them.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.580
Anyway, I love Seinfeld--

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.620
- Kramer would definitely
like, sort of like,

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.010
blow up the Mafia somehow.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.453
- Yes, it would have been a great episode.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.770
Good question!

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.940
Okay, this next one is from J Portnay,

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.080
who asks, "What is the dumbest fight

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.430
you've gotten into in quarantine?"

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:27.250
Well, you know what, here's the thing.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.080
You should never ask
a married person that.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:29.913
(laughing)

00:02:29.913 --> 00:02:32.210
- Because there's plenty.
- Right, yeah.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:35.970
- I don't even know, like
Bran and I, it's just 'cause

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:38.980
the kids are crazy, everything's crazy,

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:39.950
and all the world together,

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.370
I mean, you and your wife,
have you all just been--

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.203
- Yeah.

00:02:43.203 --> 00:02:44.480
- Stupid things.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.020
- Well I'd have to say,
well our two year old like,

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:52.750
he played, fell and hit
his chin and you know,

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:55.860
he split it open and I
immediately panicked,

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:56.930
'cause I thought we were gonna have to go

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:57.780
the emergency room,

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.010
which is obviously not a
place you wanna be right now.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:02.230
You know, because you don't wanna require

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:03.449
the attention of first responders,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.680
who are dealing with
more important things.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.680
And basically while I was flipping out

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:08.900
and screaming about how bad it was,

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:10.936
my wife just like, put a
Band-Aid on it and fixed it.

00:03:10.936 --> 00:03:12.645
(laughing)

00:03:12.645 --> 00:03:13.478
Making it very clear,

00:03:13.478 --> 00:03:15.585
that I'm not the person
you want in a crisis.

00:03:15.585 --> 00:03:16.418
(laughing)

00:03:16.418 --> 00:03:18.348
- Okay, I'm you, and my husband is her.

00:03:18.348 --> 00:03:20.800
I would have been like, "Oh my God!"

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.990
I can't even, there's not even,

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.440
we've had so many dumb
arguments, like stupid.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.467
And then we, and then literally
in a moment we're like,

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:29.307
"This is so stupid, like,
let's just go have a drink."

